+# TASK-260730-3ev75n Relux Dispatch Evidence
+
+## Scope
+
+- `relux-sample` commit `47236f2cea66a9ef7b72569d95383abf1b7d2c7d`
+- `swift-relux` commit `17efec6d94190ab318ea57cc76dabaad1fc3cf2c`
+- `swiftui-relux` commit `69fbc12f8f79a15930d78570df6fa608b0847b61`
+
+## Library contract
+
+- `swift-relux/Sources/Relux/Relux/Relux.swift` exposes
+  `Relux.shared`, constructs the application dispatcher, and rejects a second
+  `Relux` instance.
+- `Relux+Dispatcher+Interface.swift` implements top-level `action`, `actions`,
+  and `performAsync` through `Relux.shared.dispatcher._actions`.
+- `Relux+Saga.swift` implements the unqualified saga/flow instance `action` and
+  `actions` helpers through `self.dispatcher._actions`. A dispatcher injected
+  into a flow therefore remains effective without a direct
+  `dispatcher.actions` call.
+- `swiftui-relux/Sources/View+ReluxEnvironment.swift` passes `(Relux, State)` to
+  `reluxTemporal`'s `onConnect` callback after temporal registration. That
+  callback is a narrow exact-runtime boundary when the dispatched work depends
+  on the state just registered in that runtime's store.
+
+## relux-sample comparison
+
+- Application sources contain 28 dispatch call sites using unqualified
+  `action`, `actions`, or `performAsync`.
+- `relux_sample/App.swift:55` is the strongest runtime-availability example:
+  `appContent(relux:)` receives the resolved runtime, but its startup task still
+  dispatches through `await actions(.concurrently)`.
+- UI containers use unqualified helpers for concrete actions/effects, including
+  Account, AuthUI, Notes create/details/list/edit, and navigation link helpers.
+- Sagas and the Notes flow use unqualified `actions`, including serial and
+  concurrent groups of concrete actions/effects.
+- Production explicit-dispatcher references are limited to the injection seam
+  in `Notes+Business+Flow.swift`: the stored `Relux.Dispatcher`, optional
+  initializer input, and `defaultDispatcher` fallback.
+- Tests create six standalone dispatchers across the obtain/upsert/delete flow
+  suites and inject them into the flow. These are isolated harness boundaries.
+- A focused search for direct
+  `(relux|dispatcher).action(...)`/`.actions(...)` calls in application and
+  test Swift sources returned no matches (real `rg` exit code `1`).
+
+## Decision
+
+Use `action`/`actions` as the canonical application vocabulary, including
+ordinary SwiftUI startup. Inside sagas/flows, the inherited helpers preserve
+injected dispatcher identity. Document direct dispatcher calls only for
+explicit host/provider infrastructure, connection-specific temporal callbacks,
+or isolated harnesses that intentionally own an exact runtime/event bus;
+runtime reachability alone is not an exception.
+
+## Evidence commands
+
+```bash
+rg -n --glob '*.swift' \
+  'await actions?\s*(\(|\{)|performAsync\s*\{' \
+  relux_sample Packages
+
+rg -n --glob '*.swift' \
+  '\bdispatcher\b|Relux\.shared|\.dispatch\(' \
+  relux_sample Packages relux_sampleTests
+
+rg -n --glob '*.swift' \
+  '(relux|dispatcher)\.(action|actions)\s*\(' \
+  relux_sample Packages relux_sampleTests
+```
