+# TASK-260730-3ev75n Swipe2Cash Runtime And Isolation Evidence
+
+## Scope
+
+- Source tree: `/Users/alexis/src/x-platform-airdrop/ios/swipe2cash`
+- App repository commit: `bb93fe4772b0543428f484bdd791923c5d728a7e`
+- The adjacent `packages/` snapshot has no enclosing Git root, so evidence
+  identifies package files by path rather than assigning them an unsupported
+  commit.
+
+## Runtime-identity dispatch
+
+- `packages/Swipe2Cash/Sources/Swipe2Cash+ReluxProvider.swift` defines a
+  `Sendable`, `@MainActor` provider whose contract resolves an exact `Relux`.
+- `app/Targets/Swipe2Cash/Sources/App/S2CDemo+Swipe2Cash+Specifics.swift`
+  implements that provider around the host application's runtime.
+- `app/Targets/Swipe2Cash/Sources/App/S2CDemo+App.swift` resolves the
+  bootstrapped runtime before dispatching app/auth initialization directly
+  through that runtime's dispatcher. This is a lifecycle/infrastructure
+  boundary, not a convenience rule for ordinary application call sites.
+- `app/Targets/Swipe2Cash/Sources/App/S2CDemo+Content.swift` retains the
+  host-provided runtime and uses its dispatcher for app-owned analytics startup.
+- Ordinary package/UI code uses unqualified `action`, `actions`, and
+  `performAsync`; flow implementations use their inherited helpers, which
+  preserve `self.dispatcher`.
+- Integration suites such as
+  `Swipe2CashFlowDiagnosticsTests.swift`,
+  `Swipe2CashMoneyTransferFlowCommandingTests.swift`, and
+  `AuthFlowErrorHandlingTests.swift` construct
+  `Relux.Dispatcher(logger:)`, inject it into the flow, and assert events
+  recorded by that exact logger. These are isolated event-bus harnesses.
+
+## Concurrency isolation
+
+- Flows are actors, including `Swipe2Cash.Flow`,
+  `Swipe2Cash.MoneyTransfer.Flow`, `Swipe2Cash.Diagnostics.Flow`, and
+  `S2CDemo.Auth.Flow`.
+- Stateful asynchronous dependencies are actors, including
+  `TransferService`, `TransferFetcher`, `AccountBalanceService`,
+  `AccountBalanceFetcher`, `SessionFetcher`, and
+  `DiagnosticsMirrorService`.
+- Their cross-task contracts are `Sendable`, including
+  `ITransferService`, `ITransferFetcher`, `IAccountBalanceService`,
+  `IAccountBalanceFetcher`, `ICommandService`, and `ReluxProvider`.
+- Immutable/stateless value wrappers remain valid. For example,
+  `MoneyTransfer.Business.CommandService` is a struct that delegates mutable
+  session/channel ownership to injected isolated dependencies, while
+  `AnalyticsSupport.DeviceContextProvider` is a stateless struct and narrows
+  UIKit access with `MainActor.run`.
+- UI/platform ownership is main-actor isolated: HybridState/module builders,
+  SwiftUI callbacks, UIKit view-controller resolution, and the Relux provider
+  contract use `@MainActor`.
+- The synchronous SDKSSO/UIKit integration boundary is explicitly
+  `@MainActor` in `Auth+Business+MtsSSO+Module.swift`; its
+  `@unchecked Sendable` and lock-backed mutable SDK object are therefore an
+  explicit third-party adapter exception, not a general business-layer model.
+
+## Documentation rule supported by the evidence
+
+- Use top-level `action`/`actions` for ordinary code targeting the initialized
+  primary application runtime.
+- Use unqualified instance helpers inside sagas/flows so injected dispatcher
+  identity is preserved.
+- Use direct `Relux`/`Dispatcher` access only where an explicit host-provider,
+  lifecycle, temporal-connection, or isolated-harness contract owns that exact
+  runtime/event bus.
+- Prefer actors for flows, sagas, and mutable asynchronous dependencies; retain
+  immutable/stateless structs where serialized mutable ownership is absent.
+- Use `@MainActor` for UI/platform ownership and synchronous third-party
+  main-thread contracts, keeping that isolation at the adapter boundary.
+
+## Evidence commands
+
+```bash
+git rev-parse HEAD
+
+rg -n --glob '*.swift' \
+  'ReluxProvider|resolveRelux|\.dispatcher\.(action|actions)|await (action|actions)\s*(\(|\{)|performAsync\s*\{' \
+  packages app
+
+rg -n --glob '*.swift' \
+  '^\s*(public |internal |private |fileprivate )?(final )?actor\s|@MainActor|protocol .*Sendable' \
+  packages/Swipe2Cash/Sources app/Targets/Swipe2Cash/Sources
+
+rg -n -C 5 --glob '*.swift' \
+  'Relux\.Dispatcher\(|Relux\.Testing\.Logger' \
+  app/Targets/Swipe2Cash/Tests/IntegrationTests packages/Swipe2Cash/Tests
+```
